      "updated": 1791971182254,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. length() --> returns number of characters.\n\n2. charAt(int index) --> Returns character available at\nthat index .\n\n-->If index is wrong thows IndexOutOfBoundsException.\n\n3. equals() --> compares two strings lexicographically and\nreturns true or false .\n\n-->Comparision is case sensitive .\n\n\n3. equalsIgnoreCase() --> compares two strings\nlexicographically and returns true or false .\n\n-->Comparision is not case sensitive .\n\n4. compareTo()  --> campare two strings and returns\ndifference of first mismatched unicode pair . If no\nmismatch is found returns 0 .\n\n--> Comparision is case sensitive .\n\n--> Belongs to Comparable\n\n5. compareToIgnoreCase() --> Comparision is case\nsensitive .\n\n--> Belongs to String class .\n\n\n6. indexOf() -->There are two versions of indexOf() in\nString one accepts character and other string and returns\nindex of their first occurrence . Comparision is case\nsensitive .\n\n--> If not presents returns -1 . \n\n7. lastIndexOf() --> There are two versions of\nlastIndexOf() in String one accepts character and other\nstring and returns index of their last occurrence .\nComparision is case sensitive .\n\n8. subString(int start, int end) --> returns the substring\nfrom index start to index end-1 .\n\n9. subString( int start) --> returns substring from start\nto last character .\n\n10. valueOf() --> converts any type of value into String .",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. length() --> returns number of characters.\n\n2. charAt(int index) --> Returns character available at that index .\n\n-->If index is wrong thows IndexOutOfBoundsException.\n\n3. equals() --> compares two strings lexicographically and returns true or false .\n\n-->Comparision is case sensitive .\n\n\n3. equalsIgnoreCase() --> compares two strings lexicographically and returns true or false .\n\n-->Comparision is not case sensitive .\n\n4. compareTo()  --> campare two strings and returns difference of first mismatched unicode pair . If no mismatch is found returns 0 .\n\n--> Comparision is case sensitive .\n\n--> Belongs to Comparable\n\n5. compareToIgnoreCase() --> Comparision is case sensitive .\n\n--> Belongs to String class .\n\n\n6. indexOf() -->There are two versions of indexOf() in String one accepts character and other string and returns index of their first occurrence . Comparision is case sensitive .\n\n--> If not presents returns -1 . \n\n7. lastIndexOf() --> There are two versions of lastIndexOf() in String one accepts character and other string and returns index of their last occurrence . Comparision is case sensitive .\n\n8. subString(int start, int end) --> returns the substring from index start to index end-1 .\n\n9. subString( int start) --> returns substring from start to last character .\n\n10. valueOf() --> converts any type of value into String .",
